{
  "_what": "Which calls an AI makes leave a row on the person's AI activity screen, and how each row reads. One row per tool name, or per act the store itself sees (`file_kept`: any file that finished arriving, by any road, marked with the app that started sending it; such a row says `seen_by: store`): `label` is what the AI did, in plain words; `item` lists where the made or touched thing's id is found, the first present wins (`from` is `result` for what the tool answered or `input` for what the AI sent, `path` the keys into it); `title` lists where a readable name for it is found the same way; `facts` (optional) names short facts kept on the row, each a list of places read the same way (a saved file's media type), so a screen can tell kinds apart without opening the thing; `opens` is the screen that shows it (a surface id with its route input), when there is one. A new tool appears on the screen by adding its row here; nothing that records or draws changes. `keep` is how many rows each person keeps, newest first. `agent` lists where, in any call, the name of the agent acting through the app is found (an AI app can run several agents). `person_app` is how what the person does themselves on their own Trillion page is named, so it is never taken for an AI. Owned by src/activity.mjs. `failed` says when a call the tool answered still did not work (a tool run whose task ended failed): `when` lists places, read like the others, each with the values that mean it failed (`equals`); `reason` lists where its own words for why are found. A call that threw is always failed; nothing that records or draws names a tool for this. `uses` (on a mark) lists where the ids the call USED are found (a file it read or attached, the handoff it passed on, the tool it ran, the event's subject): each place is {from, path}; with `each: true` the path ends at a list or object whose members are ids, or hold one at `path_in_each`; `match` keeps only members that look like the id meant (a file's identity), for inputs whose other values are free words. `for` (top level, read in every call, plus a mark's own) lists the same way where what the call was done FOR is found (the decision behind it, what a message is about). Both are kept as links beside the row, so a trace follows them (src/activity.mjs traceActivity). `kept_with` (on a mark, or on a `uses` or `for` place) names the access (commercial-offer-records access_refs) a person must hold for the row, or the id found at that place, to be kept; a person without it keeps neither (src/activity.mjs keptActivityRow), so a free decision's goal, move and id are kept nowhere. `kept_at_once` is the most rows one request may hand the account's own record book to keep (native activity:keep): one MCP request carries at most 50 calls, each leaving at most one row.",
  "keep": 5000,
  "kept_at_once": 50,
  "agent": [
